    "summary": "Two resting goats; single-page painting on an album folio. The goats face each other. Right goat rests on all fours, with large antlers spread widely apart, while the other stands opposite, gazing above (painted with significanlty smaller antlers). Inscribed. Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk and opaque watercolour on paper. Album is bound in brown leather with gold gilt decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
